  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $14,$ the additive inverse of $-10$ modulo $14$ is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $-10$ modulo $14$ is the integer $0\\le x<14$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-10)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14).\n$$\n\nNotice that $10+(-10)≡0,$ so $x≡10\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14),$ which is already in the required form. \n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-10$ modulo $14$ is $10.$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
